clauses.text:
You can delete your account under Account. You can download your data first. After you ask, we wait {{product.deletionGraceDays}} days. If you sign in again in that time, the deletion is cancelled. When the {{product.deletionGraceDays}} days end, we delete:

- your profile (name and email) and sign-in details;
- your devices and sessions;
- your notification choices and consent history;
- your usage analytics (person and events).

We keep only the records named in section 7. If you sign up again with the same email address, the new account is empty and the kept records are not linked to it.

Deleting your account does not delete what Paddle keeps. To ask Paddle to delete or show its data, use Paddle's form at https://preferences.paddle.com or its support.

You can ask us to:

- show you the data we hold about you, and give you a copy (you can download your data as a file under Account);
- correct data that is wrong;
- delete your data;
- stop or limit how we use it;
- stop using it where we rely on legitimate interests, and move it to another service where the law gives you that right;
- withdraw consent at any time. This does not affect what we did before.

How: use the buttons under Account, or write to us on our Contact page (/contact). We may ask you to prove who you are. It costs nothing, unless a request is clearly unfounded or excessive.

How fast: we answer within 10 days (Korea) or one month (EU and UK). If we need more time or cannot do what you ask, we tell you why and how to appeal.

If you are not happy, you can complain to us first, and you can always complain to a data protection authority. In Korea these include the Personal Information Protection Commission and the Personal Information Dispute Mediation Committee. In the EU and UK, contact the authority in your country.
